{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/820149-how-fast-are-you-loyal-to-your-pack","id":820149,"title":"How fast are you loyal to your pack?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-30T21:45:06-08:00","id":820149,"title":"How fast are you loyal to your pack?","content":"So antagonist land, how fast is a werewolf loyal to their new pack after it has adopted them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T21:53:53-08:00","id":820152,"title":"","content":"It's the other way around. A pack doesn't picks you, at least not when talking about Forsaken - Pure might be a different case altogether. You pick your packmates. If you don't trust you to begin with...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T22:08:57-08:00","id":820163,"title":"","content":"well... I should clarify, this individual is joining the Predator Kings. I haven't really decided if that's his choice etc, etc, the story is simply moving in this direction. He's kind of caught up in first change fallout, and they happen to be the ones that are there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T22:36:18-08:00","id":820177,"title":"","content":"The Pure are a bit atypical an example if you use the Forsaken as a standard because there's a lot of brutal indoctrination involved. It's much like joining a cult.<br /> <br /> Mind you, joining any pack is like joining a cult, but these ones are as a rule much more likely to indulge in actual cult-like tactics consciously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T01:10:34-08:00","id":820216,"title":"","content":"Well, my take of it has always been that werewolves feel an instinctive compulsion to belong in a pack as one of their primary urges. For a werewolf, finding a pack and hunting together is the equivalent of the human desire to find a mate and raise a family together. Much like humans though, werewolves are thinking and intelligent creatures. When they're young, they might throw themselves into a pack in seconds overcome by the exciting new emotions and sensations. Older and more experienced werewolves can temper those urges because they're much more familiar with them. <br /> <br /> For young Nazusul (sp?) shortly after their first change, I imagine these confusing urges lead to all sorts of Romeo and Juliet style tragedies where they try desperately to form a pack and devote themselves to it the very moment that they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T08:47:18-08:00","id":820356,"title":"","content":"It's all going to depend on the individual, and the group. Some new wolves might take to it like a fish to water, others like a duck to water, others like a cat. Providing the Predator Kings know the new wolf is doing what they need to do they might not be too prying, but alternatively they might hassle and harangue the newcomer until they 'fit in' more.<br /> <br /> Becoming part of a pack is quick and easy, becoming loyal to it varies a hell of a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:03:05-08:00","id":820443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/820149-how-fast-are-you-loyal-to-your-pack?p=820216#post820216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my take of it has always been that werewolves feel an instinctive compulsion to belong in a pack as one of their primary urges. For a werewolf, finding a pack and hunting together is the equivalent of the human desire to find a mate and raise a family together. Much like humans though, werewolves are thinking and intelligent creatures. When they're young, they might throw themselves into a pack in seconds overcome by the exciting new emotions and sensations. Older and more experienced werewolves can temper those urges because they're much more familiar with them.<br /> <br /> For young Nazusul (sp?) shortly after their first change, I imagine these confusing urges lead to all sorts of Romeo and Juliet style tragedies where they try desperately to form a pack and devote themselves to it the very moment that they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my take, the instinct is there, but it damned well doesn't over-rides common sense. Second edition Uratha just fresh from the change? Nuzusul? They're even more human-thinking than ever. Harmony 9. Fucked if they're just gonna toss their life away because some asshole bit him and murdered his whole family (he did it himself, in fact, but denial can be a bitch).<br /> <br /> Or maybe it was the most liberating experience in his life and he can't wait for the slightless provocation to go Gauru again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 02-01-2016, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T23:24:36-08:00","id":820772,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that the entire family dynamic has changed as of 2e. Wolfblooded are part of the pack now, not just valuable breeding stock that needs to be kept in the dark and at arm's length.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T04:08:42-08:00","id":820870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/820149-how-fast-are-you-loyal-to-your-pack?p=820772#post820772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that the entire family dynamic has changed as of 2e. Wolfblooded are part of the pack now, not just valuable breeding stock that needs to be kept in the dark and at arm's length.</div> </div> </div> </div>That implication doesn't change my scenario at all. Shit happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T04:49:09-08:00","id":820886,"title":"","content":"Yeah a &quot;new pack&quot; basically <i>is</i> a new family. Generally a werewolf is either part of their pack long before they change, or they're leaving behind their old life somewhat when they join. <br /> <br /> It's not often you can just go to your family &quot;Hey, I'm a half-spirit wolf monster now. Wanna join this club for other wolf monsters + friends and family?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T05:05:45-08:00","id":820892,"title":"","content":"With the new setup, the Pure aren't just pulling people off the street to join their cause anymore after decades of 'normal living' and a month of First Change.<br /> <br /> They have wolf-blooded and humans with them, many of them probably raised from birth into the belief system they have, waiting for the day they can change and have the chains of Luna burned off them so that they can become a 'better' member of the pack instead of just an assistant in pack rites or lower 'caste' of hunter. Odds are they've been participants in hunts, too, with rites like Great Hunt or Totemic Empowerment giving them a taste of what it's like to be a true werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-01-2016, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T11:51:41-08:00","id":821105,"title":"","content":"A wolf becomes part of a pack when its totem accepts them into the pack covenant. That doesn't however guaranty loyalty, that trait would vary with the individual and their relationship with the pack. End statement being that there really is no point where loyalty is now sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T12:00:23-08:00","id":821114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/820149-how-fast-are-you-loyal-to-your-pack?p=821105#post821105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A wolf becomes part of a pack when its totem accepts them into the pack covenant. That doesn't however guaranty loyalty, that trait would vary with the individual and their relationship with the pack. End statement being that there really is no point where loyalty is now sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, totems aren't a requirement for packs anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"ke